<html xmlns:o='urn:schemas-microsoft-com:office:office' xmlns:w='urn:schemas-microsoft-com:office:word' xmlns='http://www.w3.org/TR/REC-html40'>
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<title>Package Functions and Package Content - Plumbfix</title>
<style>
@page {
    size: A4;
    margin: 1in;
}
body {
    font-family: 'Calibri', 'Arial', sans-serif;
    font-size: 11pt;
    line-height: 1.4;
    color: #222222;
}
h1 {
    font-family: 'Calibri', sans-serif;
    font-size: 18pt;
    color: #1F4E78;
    margin-top: 0;
    margin-bottom: 12pt;
    font-weight: bold;
    text-align: center;
    border-bottom: 2px solid #1F4E78;
    padding-bottom: 6px;
}
h2 {
    font-family: 'Calibri', sans-serif;
    font-size: 14pt;
    color: #1F4E78;
    margin-top: 16pt;
    margin-bottom: 8pt;
    font-weight: bold;
}
h3 {
    font-family: 'Calibri', sans-serif;
    font-size: 12pt;
    color: #2E75B6;
    margin-top: 12pt;
    margin-bottom: 6pt;
    font-weight: bold;
}
table {
    border-collapse: collapse;
    width: 100%;
    margin-bottom: 18pt;
}
th {
    background-color: #1F4E78;
    color: #FFFFFF;
    font-weight: bold;
    font-size: 11pt;
    padding: 8px 10px;
    border: 1px solid #1F4E78;
    text-align: left;
}
td {
    padding: 7px 10px;
    border: 1px solid #D9D9D9;
    font-size: 10.5pt;
    vertical-align: top;
}
tr:nth-child(even) td {
    background-color: #F2F5F8;
}
ul {
    margin: 0;
    padding-left: 18px;
}
li {
    margin-bottom: 4px;
}
</style>
</head>
<body>

<h1>Plumbfix: Plumbing Management System — Package Architecture Specification</h1>

<h2>4.1.2 Package Functions</h2>
<p>Table 4.1 shows the package functions for each architectural layer in the system.</p>

<h3>Table 4.1 Package functions</h3>
<table>
    <thead>
        <tr>
            <th style="width: 35%;">Package</th>
            <th style="width: 65%;">Package Functions</th>
        </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
        <tr>
            <td><strong>View Layer</strong><br>(SDD_PKG_100)</td>
            <td>
                <ul>
                    <li>To display user interface forms and web screens</li>
                    <li>To display dynamic data and accept input data from users</li>
                    <li>To update and validate client-side input data</li>
                    <li>To submit requests and display system feedback notifications</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td><strong>Domain Layer (Controllers)</strong><br>(SDD_PKG_200)</td>
            <td>
                <ul>
                    <li>To process system business rules and application logic</li>
                    <li>To control information flow from the view layer to the data access layer</li>
                    <li>To manage user authentication, session state, authorization, and payment processing logic</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td><strong>Data Access Layer (Eloquent Models)</strong><br>(SDD_PKG_300)</td>
            <td>
                <ul>
                    <li>To establish and maintain database connections</li>
                    <li>To represent database entity models and manage relational mappings</li>
                    <li>To execute SQL statements (retrieve, insert, update, delete) on the database</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
        </tr>
    </tbody>
</table>

